  "comment": "Shared OriginPolicy vectors. LAN 10.8.0.2 is example-ip. scripts/test-protocol.py loads this file and asserts every non-null origin string appears in OriginPolicyTests.swift. The Swift XCTest table is hand-copied, not generated. Add a vector here first, then copy the origin string into the Swift test. Empty fragment/query/userinfo rows close a urlparse-vs-URLComponents fidelity gap; those hosts are still loopback, so Python allowing them was not a security hole.",
